ull, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8eb4fc29b1ce66bf73afe9fc0495391c19e30e22", "message": "Create README.md", "created_at": "2024-08-02T10:03:27Z", "repo": "potential-fishstick", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2ce118d15784fe706c6ce44c0d82a71374f72dca", "message": "Create Recover.c\n\nThe program, recover.c, is designed to recover JPEG files from a forensic image. It scans through a raw data file, identifies the start of JPEG files by detecting specific byte patterns, and writes the recovered JPEGs to disk. Each recovered file is named sequentially using the format \"###.jpg\", where \"###\" is a zero-padded number indicating the order of recovery.\r\n\r\nThe program uses a buffer to read 512-byte blocks from the input file. It checks the first four bytes of each block to determine whether they match the signature of a JPEG file (0xff, 0xd8, 0xff, and a fourth byte with the top four bits set to 1110). When a new JPEG is detected, the previous file (if any) is closed, and a new file is created for the new JPEG data. The program ensures proper memory management and handles file I/O errors gracefully.", "created_at": "2024-08-02T10:01:04Z", "repo": "potential-fishstick", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1a35e6de348800d1fddcb88df343185e9c12c775", "message": "Update Bricks.py\n\ntypo", "created_at": "2024-07-28T05:40:31Z", "repo": "potential-fishstick", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e7171f3b45e25231cadbda4b4c304bf48f2a48d6", "message": " changed name", "created_at": "2024-07-28T05:39:25Z", "repo": "potential-fishstick", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "499437cd0067cdc688498a234783cf173747acc1", "message": " chnaged name", "created_at": "2024-07-28T05:38:33Z", "repo": "potential-fishstick", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "660e988bff31c4b4c